          "evidence": "Proof steps 2.1 and 3.1 (eventual rectangular full rank and separately established square-aspect positive-spectrum existence): The lower singular-value theorem splits subunit, superunit and square aspect using confinement and independent positive trace witnesses. A positive singular-value list could be empty for initial all-zero blocks, but the fixed-degree witness establishes eventual nonemptiness before its minimum is used.",
