      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-46",
        "notes": "Checked all four steps: one-sided truncation preserves nonpositive mean; exponential bound and finite stopping yield the stated maximal tail; r=4 makes dyadic row-union errors summable with only finite second moment. Dyadic bracketing covers arbitrary n, v=0 and C<=0 are handled, and transposition preserves iid. No independence across sizes is needed."
